---
import Icon from '../Icon.astro';
const {kind, design, offer, reviews} = Astro.props;
const imdb = [
  ['1', 'Rating + vote count', 'One compact score beside TMDB. Show vote count so a small sample does not look definitive.', 'Public datasets'],
  ['2', 'Episode ratings', 'Add a small score in the episode view. Avoid a second chart on the overview.', 'Public datasets'],
  ['3', 'Typed film connections', 'Use sequence and spin-off links in Relations; omit incidental references and spoofs.', 'Licensed bulk data'],
  ['4', 'Content guidance', 'A collapsed five-category parents guide. Spoiler-marked descriptions stay hidden.', 'Licensed data'],
  ['5', 'Credits + known-for titles', 'Fill missing credits; show two known-for titles only when opening a person.', 'Public basics; richer API licensed'],
  ['6', 'Original + regional titles', 'Useful for search and matching; keep the display title uncluttered.', 'Public datasets'],
  ['7', 'Keywords', 'At most three useful, spoiler-safe themes; put the rest in a disclosure.', 'Licensed API'],
  ['8', 'Awards', 'One notable win in expanded details. Skip long nominations lists.', 'Licensed API / datasets'],
];
---
<dialog class="lab-dialog lab-notes-dialog" id="lab-design-notes" aria-labelledby="lab-notes-title">
  <div class="lab-dialog-header"><div><p class="lab-kicker">Detail design lab</p><h2 id="lab-notes-title">The thinking behind the pages</h2></div><button type="button" data-lab-close-dialog aria-label="Close design notes"><Icon name="close"/></button></div>
  <div class="lab-notes-body">
    {kind === 'game' && <form class="lab-game-scenarios" action="/dev/details" method="get">
      <input type="hidden" name="media" value="game"/><input type="hidden" name="design" value={design}/>
      <h3>Game preview states</h3>
      <label>Price<select name="offer"><option value="sale" selected={offer === 'sale'}>On sale</option><option value="regular" selected={offer === 'regular'}>Regular price</option></select></label>
      <label>Steam reviews<select name="reviews"><option value="positive" selected={reviews === 'positive'}>Positive</option><option value="mixed" selected={reviews === 'mixed'}>Mixed</option><option value="negative" selected={reviews === 'negative'}>Negative recent reviews</option></select></label>
      <button type="submit" class="lab-primary-button">Apply preview</button>
      <p>Prices and reviews are illustrative, not live Control data. Prices are for the PC Ultimate Edition in Germany (EUR). Hover, focus or open a review summary to see its positive percentage.</p>
    </form>}
    <div class="lab-concept-notes"><article><span>01</span><h3>Folio</h3><p>A quiet catalogue: a poster and tracking rail, compact modules, and information you can find without hunting.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Marquee</h3><p>A cinematic opening with Folio’s tracking rail and compact content modules, spaced across a wider canvas.</p></article><article><span>02.5</span><h3>Marquee 2.5</h3><p>The same Marquee layout with a larger cover and the title aligned to the content column.</p></article><article><span>02.7</span><h3>Marquee - Tom</h3><p>Friends' ratings fill the wide overview column in a wrapping grid. Game pricing moves into the compact right rail; the opening and remaining content retain Marquee 2.5's layout.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Panorama</h3><p>A story-first layout: expansive artwork, an in-line tracking dock, wider editorial blocks, and fewer boxes.</p></article></div>
    <h3>IMDb additions, in priority order</h3><p>My recommendation is to start with ratings and episode scores. The rest belongs behind an intentional action.</p>
    <div class="lab-notes-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Addition</th><th>Placement</th><th>Access</th></tr></thead><tbody>{imdb.map(([rank,field,placement,access]) => <tr><td>{rank}</td><th scope="row">{field}</th><td>{placement}</td><td>{access}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <p class="lab-source-note">Public IMDb TSV datasets are refreshed daily and cover ratings, episode mapping, principal credits, names, alternate titles, and basic metadata. The richer API is licensed. The public datasets do not include posters, parents-guide text, keywords, reviews, or trivia. IMDb does not provide a general book catalogue.</p>
    <h3>Provider feasibility</h3>
    <div class="lab-notes-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Best route</th><th>Limit</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Score distribution</th><td>Aggregate AnyList users’ own ratings.</td><td>TMDB exposes average/count, not a public vote histogram. The expanded chart is explicitly sample AnyList data.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Steam scores & reviews</th><td><a href="https://partner.steamgames.com/doc/webapi/IUserReviewsService" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Valve’s IUserReviewsService / GetAppReviews</a></td><td>Public text, positive/negative totals, helpfulness and play time. Binary sentiment, not a ten-point score. Anonymous requests have a lower rate limit; cache responses.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Steam prices</th><td><a href="https://docs.isthereanydeal.com/#tag/games/operation/games-prices-v3" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">IsThereAnyDeal regional prices</a></td><td>API key; country and shop filters. Distinguish the Steam store from stores selling Steam keys. SteamDB currently offers no general public API and disallows scraping.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Similar movies / series</th><td><a href="https://developer.themoviedb.org/reference/movie-recommendations" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">TMDB recommendations</a>, with separate TV endpoint</td><td>IMDb’s free datasets have no recommendation links. Its official public API docs did not confirm access to the website’s More like this results. The preview suggestions are curated, not API responses.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Film sequence</th><td>TMDB collection parts; richer connections in licensed IMDb bulk data</td><td>Release order in a collection is an inference, not an explicit prequel/sequel graph. Licensed IMDb movieConnections has typed links, but excludes a general book catalogue.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Game relations</th><td><a href="https://api-docs.igdb.com/#game" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">IGDB parent games, expansions, remakes and collections</a></td><td>Requires Twitch credentials. Collection membership alone does not establish the immediate sequel. Shared-universe links may need curation.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Books & cross-media adaptations</th><td><a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Property:P155" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Wikidata follows</a> and <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Property:P144" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">based on</a>, with provider IDs</td><td>Useful open typed relationships; coverage varies. Open Library supplies book metadata/covers, not a complete ordered adaptation graph.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>Relations prioritizes previous/next entries, then source/adaptation, then other connections. Only genuine relationships appear. Severance has no relation fixtures, so the section is absent. Unknown connections should stay absent rather than be guessed.</p>
    <div class="lab-notes-columns"><section><h3>Extensions shown in the mockups</h3><ul><li>Games and books with their own metadata adapters.</li><li>Edition-specific page totals and recorded play time.</li><li>Private notes, separate from the existing list-visible notes.</li><li>Automatic next-unwatched episode selection.</li><li>Spoiler-safe titles and stills for unwatched episodes.</li><li>Cast portraits, linked credits, and a deduplicated artwork lightbox.</li><li>Typed cross-media Relations and a separate Similar section.</li><li>Expandable AnyList score distributions.</li></ul></section><section><h3>Already present in some form</h3><ul><li>The actual AnyList topbar and navigation.</li><li>List statuses, progress, favorites, and quick ratings.</li><li>Add to library for films and series.</li><li>Independent season ratings and the rated-season average.</li><li>People-you-follow scores.</li><li>Film and TV facts, posters, and backdrops.</li><li>Season metadata and season-wide watched actions.</li></ul><p>These previews use isolated browser storage. They do not write to your account or call the tracking API.</p></section></div>
    <h3>Where the data comes from</h3><p>Film and TV fields match TMDB’s API: overview, genres, release dates, runtime, seasons, episode titles/stills, credits, images, votes, and collections. Scores, vote counts, progress, notes, and friends are sample data. Season 2 uses illustrative runtimes and neutral image placeholders where no distinct still was selected.</p><p>TMDB does not catalogue books or games. Control uses real Steam screenshots; Dune uses Open Library’s ISBN cover and edition fields. The book’s banner is explicitly film-adaptation artwork; it appears last in the artwork gallery. Relations are manually selected genuine connections, not fetched edges. The previous shelf suggestions have been removed from Relations.</p>
    <nav class="lab-notes-sources" aria-label="Design research sources"><a href="https://developer.themoviedb.org/reference/collection-details" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">TMDB collections</a><a href="https://data.imdb.com/non-commercial-datasets/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">IMDb public datasets</a><a href="https://data.imdb.com/documentation/api-documentation/sample-queries/title-name" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">IMDb API fields</a><a href="https://data.imdb.com/documentation/bulk-data-documentation/data-dictionary/titles/#movieconnections" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">IMDb connections</a><a href="https://steamdb.info/faq/#does-steamdb-have-an-api" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SteamDB API policy</a><a href="https://anilist.co/anime/189046/ReZERO-Starting-Life-in-Another-World-Season-4/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">AniList reference</a></nav>
    <button class="lab-text-button" data-lab-action="reset" type="button">Reset this media’s preview state <Icon name="undo"/></button>
  </div>
</dialog>
